  "name": "Fix kanban issues",
  "pinned": false,
  "description": "## Summary\n\n1. **Root Cause**: The Kanban component was polluting store data by attaching view-only properties (`tasks`, `valid`, `position`, `project`) directly onto store kanban board/column objects, causing those fields to be persisted on `saveKanban()`.\n\n2. **Fix Strategy**: Enforced a strict separation between **store data** (raw scalar config) and **component view data** (enriched objects used only for rendering).\n\n3. **Key Refactor**: Replaced `filteredColumns` with `viewColumns` and `buildColumns()` with `buildViewColumns()`, which creates fresh plain objects from store config without mutating the originals.\n\n4. **Persistence Fix**: `onColumnTaskListChanged()` was updated to write back only safe scalar config fields and chat ID order \u2014 never view-only enriched fields.\n\n5. **Computed Properties**: Split `boards`/`activeBoard` into `rawBoards` (pure store config) and view-enriched versions, ensuring `saveKanban()` never serializes computed view data like task arrays.",
